From: mojito-mainline <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: edt-ft5x06 - read all 10 points on the FT5452

The FT5452 in the Redmi Note 10 (mojito) only advances its touch table
after the host reads the full 63-byte, 10-point frame, as the vendor fts
driver does. With the 5-point read the chip keeps raising its interrupt,
reports a stale contact and never signals the release.

Signed-off-by: mojito-mainline <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c	2026-11-26 11:58:10.788344166 +0500
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c	2026-11-26 11:58:10.820194347 +0500
@@ -1459,7 +1459,12 @@
 };
 
 static const struct edt_i2c_chip_data edt_ft5452_data = {
-	.max_support_points = 5,
+	/*
+	 * The Redmi Note 10 panel's FT5452 keeps reporting a stale contact and
+	 * never releases it unless the whole 10-point frame (63 bytes) is read,
+	 * as the vendor driver does.
+	 */
+	.max_support_points = 10,
 };
 
 static const struct edt_i2c_chip_data edt_ft5506_data = {
